-- title:
--   Gonflement and completion at a prime of a noetherian ring
-- statement:
--   Let $S$ be a commutative noetherian ring (a type in the lowest universe) and let $\mathfrak p$ be a point of the prime spectrum of $S$, with underlying prime ideal $\mathfrak p.\mathrm{asIdeal}$. The assertion is the existence of a type $R$ carrying a commutative ring structure for which: $R$ is local; $R$ is noetherian; $R$ is complete and separated for the adic filtration given by its maximal ideal $\mathfrak m_R$ (`IsAdicComplete`); the residue field $R/\mathfrak m_R$ is algebraically closed; and $R$ is simultaneously an $S$-algebra and an algebra over the localisation $S_{\mathfrak p} =$ `Localization.AtPrime 𝔭.asIdeal`, these two structures being compatible in the sense that $S \to S_{\mathfrak p} \to R$ is a tower of scalars (`IsScalarTower`). Finally, the conclusion asserted of this data is that $R$ is faithfully flat as a module over $S_{\mathfrak p}$. All the structures and instances are produced existentially, so the statement provides no control over $R$ beyond the listed properties; in particular nothing is claimed about the maximal ideal of $R$ being generated by that of $S_{\mathfrak p}$, nor about the residue field being the algebraic closure of $\kappa(\mathfrak p)$.
--
--   This is the commutative-algebra input usually called gonflement (Grothendieck, EGA $0_{\mathrm{III}}$ 10.3.1), followed by adic completion: every local ring of a noetherian ring admits a faithfully flat complete local noetherian extension with algebraically closed residue field. It is used in the noetherian spreading step for canonical polarisation data of fake elliptic curves, where a datum known to exist over all complete local noetherian rings with algebraically closed residue field must be propagated to an arbitrary noetherian base.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsNoetherianRing_exists_faithfullyFlat_isAdicComplete_isAlgClosed_residueField_atPrime.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

theorem IsNoetherianRing.exists_faithfullyFlat_isAdicComplete_isAlgClosed_residueField_atPrime
    (S : Type) [CommRing S] [IsNoetherianRing S] (𝔭 : PrimeSpectrum S) :
    ∃ (R : Type) (_ : CommRing R) (_ : IsLocalRing R) (_ : IsNoetherianRing R)
      (_ : IsAdicComplete (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R) R) (_ : IsAlgClosed (IsLocalRing.ResidueField R))
      (_ : Algebra S R) (_ : Algebra (Localization.AtPrime 𝔭.asIdeal) R)
      (_ : IsScalarTower S (Localization.AtPrime 𝔭.asIdeal) R),
      Module.FaithfullyFlat (Localization.AtPrime 𝔭.asIdeal) R := by sorry
